01:42:32.480 --> 01:42:35.490
Like, I really don't like talking about that.

2614
01:42:35.490 --> 01:42:38.080
And that doesn't feel good.

2615
01:42:38.080 --> 01:42:40.650
Like that was not a fun part of this conversation for me.

2616
01:42:40.650 --> 01:42:45.040
And if, like, to me, that's the essence of vulnerability.

2617
01:42:45.040 --> 01:42:47.930
Like if I wanna live that value, it shouldn't feel good.

2618
01:42:47.930 --> 01:42:49.987
Whereas if I'm all calculating and I'm like,

2619
01:42:49.987 --> 01:42:51.160
"Oh, like that's gonna make,"

2620
01:42:51.160 --> 01:42:51.993
I don't, people are gonna,

2621
01:42:51.993 --> 01:42:53.840
a lot of people probably tune out at that point.

2622
01:42:53.840 --> 01:42:55.245
Like, "This guy's nuts."

2623
01:42:55.245 --> 01:42:58.830
But I think that that's like that for me is the barometer.

2624
01:42:58.830 --> 01:43:02.430
If you are doing vulnerability as a means to an end

2625
01:43:02.430 --> 01:43:03.420
or like you're scheming,

2626
01:43:03.420 --> 01:43:05.170
then you're probably

2627
01:43:05.170 --> 01:43:08.140
actually doing yourself more harm than good.

2628
01:43:08.140 --> 01:43:09.090
At some point,

2629
01:43:09.090 --> 01:43:12.110
if you're compelled to tell that story tons of times

2630
01:43:12.110 --> 01:43:14.890
cause you're doing lots of media and podcasts,

2631
01:43:14.890 --> 01:43:17.670
you'll probably end up in this place where I found myself,

2632
01:43:17.670 --> 01:43:20.440
which is telling the same story again.

2633
01:43:20.440 --> 01:43:21.273
And always trying to,

2634
01:43:21.273 --> 01:43:23.470
you know, be as honest as possible

2635
01:43:23.470 --> 01:43:27.790
and perhaps, you know, find a different way into it

2636
01:43:27.790 --> 01:43:30.750
or a different version of it or angle of it.

2637
01:43:30.750 --> 01:43:33.620
But I found myself telling a story that's true

2638
01:43:33.620 --> 01:43:35.840
and then wondering like, "Did that really happen?"

2639
01:43:35.840 --> 01:43:38.380
Because you, you end up disassociating with it

2640
01:43:38.380 --> 01:43:40.140
because you've told it so many times

2641
01:43:40.140 --> 01:43:42.550
and then you're like, and it doesn't have that same,

2642
01:43:42.550 --> 01:43:46.103
you don't feel like it's it's vulnerability because,

2643
01:43:47.600 --> 01:43:49.400
because it's so rote at that point

2644
01:43:49.400 --> 01:43:52.760
and then it feels rehearsed and almost flat.

2645
01:43:52.760 --> 01:43:55.010
And I'm like, "Did that even happen? Like it?

2646
01:43:55.010 --> 01:43:56.580
Or am I just remembering this?

2647
01:43:56.580 --> 01:43:58.210
Like what is the truth behind this?"

2648
01:43:58.210 --> 01:44:02.550
So then it becomes an exercise of like going deeper into it

2649
01:44:02.550 --> 01:44:03.470
and trying to find a way

2650
01:44:03.470 --> 01:44:06.790
to continue to stay emotionally connected with that thing

2651
01:44:06.790 --> 01:44:09.600
that was so formative and kind of,

2652
01:44:09.600 --> 01:44:11.770
you know, catalyzing journey that you've bet on.

2653
01:44:11.770 --> 01:44:12.900
And just painful.

2654
01:44:12.900 --> 01:44:14.158
Yeah.

2655
01:44:14.158 --> 01:44:16.160
And I think that's it, like if it feel,

